From: Yongkui Yang <yongkuiy@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hab: avoid MM_ID_MAX collision with kernel 7.0 mm_types.h

Kernel 7.0's MM_ID_MAX in <linux/mm_types.h> overrides HAB's MM_ID_MAX
(1903), making HABCFG_MMID_AREA_MAX 21474836 instead of 19 and inflating
msm_hab.ko to 2.6 GB. Use a private HAB_MM_ID_MAX instead.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Yongkui Yang <yongkuiy@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 hab.c | 2 +-
 hab.h | 5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hab.h b/hab.h
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/hab.h
+++ b/hab.h
@@ -7,6 +7,9 @@
 #define __HAB_H

 #include "hab_os.h"	/* OS-specific part in the core header file */
+
+/* Private name for habmmid.h's MM_ID_MAX: kernel 7.0 mm_types.h redefines it. */
+#define HAB_MM_ID_MAX 1903

 #ifdef CONFIG_MSM_VHOST_HAB
 #define spin_lock_bh spin_lock
@@ -99,7 +102,7 @@
 #define MAX_EXP_PAYLOAD_COUNT 0xFFFFF

 #define HABCFG_FILE_SIZE_MAX   256
-#define HABCFG_MMID_AREA_MAX   (MM_ID_MAX/100)
+#define HABCFG_MMID_AREA_MAX   (HAB_MM_ID_MAX/100)

 #define HABCFG_VMID_MAX        16
 #define HABCFG_VMID_INVALID    (-1)
diff --git a/hab.c b/hab.c
index 2345678..bcdefgh 100644
--- a/hab.c
+++ b/hab.c
@@ -1246,7 +1246,7 @@ int do_hab_parse(void)
 		pr_err("hab config open failed, prepare default gvm %d settings\n",
 				default_gvmid);
 		(void)fill_default_gvm_settings(&hab_driver.settings, default_gvmid,
-				MM_AUD_START, MM_ID_MAX);
+				MM_AUD_START, HAB_MM_ID_MAX);
 	}

 	/* now generate hab pchan list */
--
2.43.0
